From 2e35320f30dc9af61267ae7f2ba853c24ce13665 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: YahiaAngelo <yahia.mostafa.elsayed@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 16:59:31 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 2/8] vphone-ev: translation, SPRR/GXF flush and ASID reuse
 diagnostics

More VPHONE_EVENT_STATS counters (off by default):
- tb_first / tb_again_samekey / tb_again_variant: whether a translation's
  guest physical PC was translated before, with the same flags (redone after
  a TB flush) or other ones; tb_crosspage, tb_race (tb_link_page found an
  existing TB), tb_oneinsn, tb_inval, tb_inval_dma_calls, tb_flush;
- range_full_size / range_full_large / page_full_large: range and page
  flushes escalated to whole-index flushes; flushidx_all/one/other;
- sprr_el0_flush, sprr_el1_flush, gxf_eret_flush: TLB flushes from Apple
  SPRR permission changes and GXF erets;
- asid_recent8 / asid_sprr_recent8: switches to one of the last 8 ASIDs.

Findings on the iPhone Duo (iOS 27.1): 33-50% of translations during boot and
app launches redo a TB lost to a full TB flush (the 2 GB code buffer fills
every 1-2 minutes: median TB 2 guest instructions, ~300 host bytes); 61-72%
of ASID switches return to one of the last 8 ASIDs.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01N89PWg24VJrcxX3MuUo4uM
